# Feature: one observable, LOCAL in one local function and GLOBAL in
#          another, and a bare observable whose value MOVES during the run.
# Tests:   `Aoff` is applied to the tag in lfA and written bare in lfB:
#            lfA(x) = ka*Aoff(x)          -> per-instance, always 1
#            lfB(x) = kb*Aoff*Boff(x)     -> system-wide count of A(m~0)
#          BNG2 resolves exactly that split in its network, keeping the
#          bare reference as a live global and collapsing the tagged one:
#            _RA_local1  ka*1
#            _RB_local1() ((kb*Aoff)*1)
#          Two things follow that ft_local_fcn_global_obs cannot reach:
#            1. RM holds one eval slot per observable, so the union of the
#               per-function local sets cannot stand in for them here — the
#               localized `Aoff` would leak into lfB, which wants the
#               global count.  Each function has to be given its own view.
#            2. `Aoff` decays as RA fires, so RB's rate changes for every B
#               instance while nothing in any B's own neighbourhood does.
#               The affected-molecule delta path cannot see that; the rule
#               needs a rescan per event or every B keeps a stale rate.
#
# Oracle:  BNG2 network -> ODE, exactly.  Both failure modes are far
#          outside sampling noise at these counts:
#            - union scoping:  lfB reads Aoff = 0 at a B molecule, RB never
#                              fires, Boff stays flat at 200.
#            - stale rate:     RB keeps firing at the seed Aoff = 200, so
#                              Boff(100) = 200*exp(-kb*200*100) = 27.1
#                              instead of 56.5.
#          Single molecules only, no complexes, so context multiplicity
#          (issue #33) cannot reach either arm.
#
# Tier:    network-free.
# Expected:
#            RA  ka*Aoff(x) = ka*1 = 0.01 per A(m~0)
#                Aoff(t) = 200*exp(-0.01 t);            Aoff(100) = 73.6
#            RB  kb*Aoff*Boff(x) = kb*Aoff(t)*1
#                Boff(t) = 200*exp(-kb*Integral(Aoff))
#                        = 200*exp(-2*(1-exp(-0.01 t)))
#                                                       Boff(100) = 56.5
#          Aoff enters RB's rate linearly and stays a large count, so the
#          stochastic mean tracks the ODE to well under a percent.
# invariant: nonneg (both species deplete; nothing is conserved)

begin model
begin parameters
    ka  1.0e-2
    kb  1.0e-4
end parameters

begin molecule types
    A(m~0~1)
    B(m~0~1)
end molecule types

begin seed species
    A(m~0)  200
    B(m~0)  200
end seed species

begin observables
    # Local in lfA (applied to the tag), global in lfB (written bare).
    Molecules  Aoff  A(m~0)
    Molecules  Boff  B(m~0)
end observables

begin functions
    lfA(x) = ka*Aoff(x)
    lfB(x) = kb*Aoff*Boff(x)
end functions

begin reaction rules
    RA: A(m~0)%x -> A(m~1)   lfA(x)
    RB: B(m~0)%x -> B(m~1)   lfB(x)
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
simulate({method=>"nf",t_end=>100,n_steps=>100})
end actions
